Subject: [PATCH] DeepSeek vision: add opt-in TensorFold arithmetic compatibility

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm
19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus the recorded 1107 series.

Rationale: TensorFold's byte-matched served lane constructs the existing
DeepSeek RoPE expression on CUDA, widens BF16-rounded vision Q/K/V values to
FP32, runs PyTorch memory-efficient attention, and rounds once before WO.
The local 65x103 fixture's CUDA-built RoPE matched TensorFold byte-for-byte:
cos 2de6257af4ec7f2e0279c71c3d0162db824b7ed7cbae9a6a8f0e25b306a34925
and sin 210e00fc3e2ae6b2f69c08e8b8c3b3e6ed10800b1cda7d088e7aabaf3c807a8e.
Keep vLLM's current CPU-built RoPE and generic attention as the default; expose
the combined arithmetic only as an explicit option for controlled parity tests.

Quality: opt-in and vision-only; enabling it changes vision embeddings and may
increase vision memory and latency. Text and the default vision path are
unchanged. The RoPE hashes prove only that boundary, not final output parity.

Provenance: the generic tower is vLLM Apache-2.0 code ported from DeepSeek's MIT
reference. Attention behavior is adapted from bertholomus/TensorFold commit
6062066f65a05a7799c09b9aadde0517ded82105 (Apache-2.0), whose attention
kernel is attributed to PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause). Device-explicit RoPE is a local,
AI-assisted adaptation of the expression already present in vLLM, verified by
local raw-stage probes. No TensorFold source or binary is copied.

Tests: focused CPU unit tests prepared for opt-in device propagation, explicit
RoPE tensor construction, FP32 efficient attention, and unchanged defaults;
not run in this source-edit step.
Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted or represented as PR-ready.
